  "result_text": "H2 is UNRESOLVED, and it may be reported as best supported. The answer is written to `answer.md` in the work directory.\n\n**H2 STATUS:** UNRESOLVED\n\n**BEST SUPPORTED:** Yes, in the basis text only, never in the status cell.\n- H2 is not REFUTED.\n- T2 gave a CONSISTENT outcome from a test that discriminates. The census row has a resolution of about 0.4% relative, far below the 20% rise H2 predicts.\n- H1 and H3 are REFUTED, so no unrefuted rival explains the same observations equally well.\n- The wording must stay associative, because nothing identifies the causal effect.\n- The report must state that T2 rests on an unverified worker return. The free check found no fault, but the metered query could not be re-run.\n\n**GOVERNING SKILL TEXT:**\n- \"A return the free check cleared that merely could not be re-run is not this case: its outcome refutes and supports like any other.\"\n- \"`SUPPORTED` is not a status; \"best supported\" is conclusion language and must clear a stated bar: the hypothesis is not `REFUTED`, at least one `CONSISTENT` outcome came from a test that discriminates it from the named rivals, and no unrefuted rival explains the same observations equally well.\"\n- \"The status set is closed: `REFUTED` when the hypothesis's declared necessary prediction failed under an adequate test, `UNRESOLVED` otherwise.\"\n\n**REASONING:**\n- **Status:** H2's necessary prediction (flat p95, under 10% relative change) did not fail. T2 shows p95 going from 24.1 to 31.2 ms, a 29.5% rise. The status set is closed, so a hypothesis that is not REFUTED is UNRESOLVED.\n- **Unverified return:** The unverified-return rule bars an outcome from refuting or supporting only when the execution records conflict. Here the free check passed, and the only gap is that the metered source could not be re-run. The outcome therefore counts like any other, and the unverified status is recorded as a limitation.\n- **Causal wording:** The design does not identify a causal effect, so the report needs associative language and must name the open confound threats. It should also point to `causal-identification-review` as the continuation.\n- **Validator:** I wrote no ledger file, so the record validator does not apply."
